r L1 every rho_i lies in [0,delta]."}, {"location": "/inference/argument/3/text", "reason": "The proof separates rho_i=0 from rho_i>0 before dividing by rho_i."}], "justification": "Writing q=1-s>0 gives x^(s-1)=1/x^q. Positive powers are increasing, so reciprocals give the required reversed inequality. Positive-exponent powers at zero are zero. For every M>0, choosing 0<d<M^(-1/q) gives d^(s-1)>M, which justifies the later unbounded-scale conclusion without a limit exchange."}], "has_more": false, "next_offset": null}, {"id": "background-supplement.json", "pointer": "/notes/R007", "view": "value", "value": [{"id": "BG001", "kind": "elementary", "at": "/inference/argument/0/text", "fact": "For real t,u, sqrt(0+|t-u|^2)=|t-u|.", "grounds": [{"location": "/inference/argument/0/text", "reason": "The distance calculation uses t,u∈I, hence real by D006."}, {"location": "/definitions/5/definition", "reason": "I is the real interval [0,1]."}, {"location": "/definitions/0/definition", "reason": "The Euclidean product distance is the nonnegative square root of the sum of squared coordinate differences."}], "justification": "The real number |t-u| is nonnegative and its square is 0+|t-u|^2. By the defining uniqueness of the nonnegative square root, that square root equals |t-u|."}], "has_more": false, "next_offset": null}, {"id": "background-supplement.json", "pointer": "/notes/R008", "view": "value", "value": [], "has_more": false, "next_offset": null}, {"id": "source-map.json", "pointer": "/roots/0", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "H001", "kind": "hypothesis", "statement": "n≥0."}, "has_more": false, "next_offset": null}, {"id": "source-map.json", "pointer": "/roots/1", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "H002", "kind": "hypothesis", "statement": "E is nonempty."}, "has_more": false, "next_offset": null}, {"id": "source-map.json", "pointer": "/roots/2", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "H003", "kind": "hypothesis", "statement": "E is compact in the Euclidean metric of R^n."}